            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 1)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "5627dc6e-c943-439e-ab4a-4531b7f24264"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Historical Background</strong><br>\nThe conflict between Israel and Palestine has deep-rooted historical origins. The region, known as the Holy Land, is significant for many religious groups. The founding of the State of Israel in the 20th century led to tensions and conflicts with Palestinian Arabs and the surrounding Arab states.</p>\n\n<p><strong>One-State Solution</strong><br>\nThe one-state solution refers to a single sovereign state that includes both Israelis and Palestinians. Advocates argue that this could provide a way to ensure the rights and freedoms of all citizens regardless of their ethnicity or religion. Critics, however, fear that a one-state solution could jeopardize the identity and security of the Jewish and Palestinian communities.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Two-State Solution</strong><br>\nThe two-state solution is a widely accepted international norm and refers to the existence of two separate states - Israel and Palestine. This solution aims to provide both peoples with self-determination and sovereign statehood. However, there are challenges concerning the precise border demarcation and security concerns of both parties.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 4.415011037527593,
            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Three-State Solution</strong><br>\nA less-known three-state solution could involve the establishment of three separate states: Israel, West Bank, and Gaza Strip. This could be a way to recognize the different political and social conditions in these areas. Yet, it is uncertain whether this solution could promote long-term stability and security in the region.</p>\n\n<p><strong>International Involvement</strong><br>\nInternational actors play an important role in the Israeli-Palestinian conflict. The United Nations, the USA, and other countries have tried to mediate and find solutions. However, their efforts are often hampered by geopolitical interests and the complexity of the conflict.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Impact of the Conflict</strong><br>\nThe conflict has profound effects on the people in the region. It leads to loss of life, displacement, economic difficulties, and a lack of political stability. The psychological impact of the conflict on the affected communities is also significant.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
